# Tool Conventions

## Use Entity Input Types

Tool handler methods must use `Create<Name>EntityInput` and `Update<Name>EntityInput` from the entity file for their argument types instead of duplicating fields inline.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — fields duplicated in the handler signature
async createCharacter(args: {
  firstName: string;
  lastName: string;
  title: string;
  age: number;
  sex: Sex;
  personality: string;
  backstory: string;
}) { ... }

// ✅ GOOD — reuse the entity input type
import { CreateCharacterEntityInput } from './character.entity';

async createCharacter(args: CreateCharacterEntityInput) { ... }

// ✅ GOOD — update handler
import { UpdateCharacterEntityInput } from './character.entity';

async updateCharacter({ id, ...dto }: UpdateCharacterEntityInput) { ... }
```

## Zod: Preferred Methods

Use the modern Zod methods. Never use their deprecated equivalents.

| ✅ Use | ❌ Deprecated |
|---|---|
| `z.uuid()` | `z.string().uuid()` |
| `z.enum(MyEnum)` | `z.nativeEnum(MyEnum)` |

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
parameters: z.object({
  id: z.string().uuid(),
  sex: z.nativeEnum(Sex),
})

// ✅ GOOD
parameters: z.object({
  id: z.uuid(),
  sex: z.enum(Sex),
})
```
